{{Stub Dialogue}}
===Head to Styxia{{subst:void|<!--104061001-->}}===
{{Mission Description|type=trailblaze|location="Warbling Shores" Styxia|Why would a father sacrifice his daughter? Why would a daughter slay her mother? Why do gods torment mortals? Why would an eagle cast a tortoise shell upon a poet's head?<br />In countless poems of the wine god, people rage, grieve, and despair. It was because the roots of these tragedies are elusive and impassive, beyond the reach of blade or noose. Just as sailors cannot slay the sea.}}
{{Dialogue Start}}

----
:'''(Trailblazer):''' (Is this... Styxia? What happened to this place...?)
:'''(Trailblazer):''' (I need to find the entrance to the Vortex guarded by the demigod of Ocean. Hysilens... is she still there?)
:'''???:''' Long time no see, Trailblazer.
:'''Lygus's Voice:''' Generation after generation of Chrysos Heir heroes have tried to defy fate with their blood and tears, either voluntarily shattering their souls or waiting in eternal solitude...
:'''Lygus's Voice:''' But alas, fate can never be defeated.
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} You again!?
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} You... managed to break free?
:'''Lygus's Voice:''' Reason and Trickery may bind my flesh, but my will shall never fall silent.
:'''Lygus's Voice:''' So, the demigod of Ocean, the Dux Gladiorum, Hysilens, sought to bring me into a fantasia with her voice and drown a genius in slumber...
:'''Lygus's Voice:''' But alas, it was all a hopeless dream. That warden fell before I did due to erosion of time, while her prisoner remained unchanged.
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} And yet, here you are, bound to this place.
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} But you have yet to taste freedom.
:'''Lygus's Voice:''' Heh, true. I can't leave this place, but what of it?
:'''Lygus's Voice:''' You should have heard of this fable. "In a shadowed cave lived a people, imprisoned from childhood and chained so that their legs and necks are fixed, forcing them not to look around at the cave, each other, or themselves."
:'''Lygus's Voice:''' "Behind them is a fire, and before them loomed the stone wall of the cave. The flames cast shadows, while the rocky surface threw back echoes..."
:'''Lygus's Voice:''' "To them, that false play is the whole world."
:'''Lygus's Voice:''' Yes, I'm trapped in the cave, but I know it's all just a fleeting illusion. I don't struggle in dreams. I wait.
:'''Lygus's Voice:''' And now, my deliverer has come. To defeat me and save this world that never owed you anything, you'll need to awaken the singer here and unseal the prison called Vortex of Genesis...
:'''Lygus's Voice:''' You'll be the one to unshackle me and bring the cave crashing down.
:'''Lygus's Voice:''' Of course, I don't mind waiting a little longer. Let me guide you through this next illusion, one last memory from that prison warden.
:'''Lygus's Voice:''' I hope you'll watch the stories of this fantasia closely. Logically, the Deliverer must see the world for what it truly is. Emotionally, this memory captures the fate of everyone in Amphoreus better than anything else...
:'''Lygus's Voice:''' Only by feeling it for yourself can you understand my point of view:
:'''Lygus's Voice:''' The meaning of "Destruction."
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} And I'll be the one to bring destruction to your scheme.
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Spare me the clichés.
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} I don't need to understand you.
:'''Lygus's Voice:''' To your unshakable resolve, I salute you. But before we step onto the final stage, let me ask you this, in the spirit of that fable I told you just now...
:{{tx}}
{{Dialogue End}}

